// The facerig package: a face that is alive, for any face mesh described by
// data. A program reaches it with 'import facerig'.
//
// WHAT IT IS. A rig is a recipe for turning a few numbers (which muscles are
// pulling, where the eyes look, what is being said) into the deformation of a
// face. Industry practice splits it three ways, and so does this package:
//
//   1. THE VOCABULARY: FACS (Facial Action Coding System, Ekman and Friesen
//      1978), the standard list of visible muscle movements, "action units"
//      (AUs): AU1 inner brow raiser, AU12 lip corner puller. A face expression
//      is a set of AUs with intensities. (units.cone)
//   2. THE SHAPES: each AU is a morph target (blend shape) of the mesh: a
//      stored displacement, mixed in by weight, the way glTF, Unreal, Unity
//      and Godot do it. Here the targets are not sculpted but BUILT, from the
//      unit table and a FaceSpec (landmarks and sizes, as data), by rules that
//      act near a landmark (targets.cone). The same table makes the targets of
//      any face that has a spec. (spec.cone)
//   3. THE LIFE: clocks and models that move the numbers: blinks on a natural
//      schedule, eyes that saccade and the head that follows, expressions
//      blended and eased, lip sync from text or phonemes, and the small
//      continual motion that keeps a face at rest alive. (blink.cone,
//      gaze.cone, speech.cone, rig.cone)
//
// THE OUTPUT of a frame is a 'FaceFrame': one weight per morph target (the
// buffer render's morph pre-pass takes), the jaw's rotation, each eyeball's
// rotation, and a small head turn. Bones for the jaw and eyes are added to a
// bonepose skeleton by 'attachFace' (bind.cone), so a face rides on a body.
// A procedural test head with a spec, skin weights, eyes, teeth and a
// texture is in testhead.cone.
//
// Conventions are bonepose's: right-handed, y up, metres, f32; a being faces
// -z; its right is +x; a positive yaw turns it to its left, a positive pitch
// looks up. Landmark names end in L or R for the being's left (-x) or right.
//
//   spec.cone      FaceSpec, Influence, UnitDef: the face as data
//   units.cone     the FACS unit table and the standard expressions
//   targets.cone   morph targets built from a mesh, a spec and the table
//   rng.cone       a seeded random source and smooth noise
//   blink.cone     the blink: schedule, profile, partial and double blinks
//   gaze.cone      eyes and head: saccades, vergence, eye-head coordination
//   speech.cone    visemes, phonemes and the lip-sync timeline (Cohen and Massaro)
//   g2p.cone       letters to phonemes, for English text
//   rig.cone       FaceRig: the clocks and blends composed into a FaceFrame
//   bind.cone      the jaw and eye bones on a skeleton
//   testhead.cone  a procedural head to test and show it on

mod facerig;

import libc;
import collections use *;
import geomath use *;
import bonepose use *;
import mesh use Mesh;
